# Git LFS support for model weights (see docs/weights.md).
#
# Both checkpoints are committed via Git LFS. Hugging Face auto-fetch is a
# second, independent channel (src/mats/weights.py, _HF_REPO_ID) -- Git LFS
# exists in parallel because our primary collaborators (USDA) cannot reach
# huggingface.co, so LFS is not optional infrastructure for them.
#
# weights/rf_detr_marker.pth (~134 MB) is fetched on every `git clone` -- it's
# mandatory for both segmentation paths, so a checkout should be immediately
# runnable without an extra download step.
#
# weights/birefnet_leaf.pth (~2.65 GB) is committed but excluded from the
# default clone/fetch via .lfsconfig (lfs.fetchexclude) -- it's optional, and
# committing it without the exclusion would force every `git clone` to
# download 2.65 GB and spend the repo's LFS bandwidth quota. Fetch it via the
# "BiRefNet setup" page in the app, or:
#   git lfs pull --include="weights/birefnet_leaf.pth"
weights/*.pth filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
